// ProjectDeliveryS708 — Sprint 708: Implement D0476 through dcVerifyLadderStopsAtTheFirstRed: `keel verify` runs the pre-commit checks as one ladder in cost order - gate validate, gate guard (from its receipt, D0371), cargo clippy -D warnings, the D0388 probe pair named by --probe, then suite --touched (keyed per D0474) - and stops at the first red, writing one receipt that names the rung. The pain: in sprint705 a clippy lint was found after a 20-minute test run because the five checks ran as separate commands in no enforced order, and with the verifier suspended (single-agent mode) the order was the AI's discipline alone - manual vigilance is not a control (D0047). The panel of 2026-09-13 ranked this third: a sequence is not a mechanism until it is one command. Chartered by D0476 (process-change, accepted by the human 2026-09-14). 3 pts.. EXECUTE. 3 pts.
package ProjectDeliveryS708 {
