    part verifyLadderStopsAtTheFirstRedStory : Story {
        :>> id = "c9618658-4bd7-4f23-be18-b8376392d611";
        :>> title = "Sprint 708: Implement D0476 through dcVerifyLadderStopsAtTheFirstRed: `keel verify` runs the pre-commit checks as one ladder in cost order - gate validate, gate guard (from its receipt, D0371), cargo clippy -D warnings, the D0388 probe pair named by --probe, then suite --touched (keyed per D0474) - and stops at the first red, writing one receipt that names the rung. The pain: in sprint705 a clippy lint was found after a 20-minute test run because the five checks ran as separate commands in no enforced order, and with the verifier suspended (single-agent mode) the order was the AI's discipline alone - manual vigilance is not a control (D0047). The panel of 2026-09-13 ranked this third: a sequence is not a mechanism until it is one command. Chartered by D0476 (process-change, accepted by the human 2026-09-14). 3 pts. (3 pts)";
        :>> createdAt = "2026-09-14"; :>> createdBy = "claudeFable5"; :>> kind = WorkKind::code; :>> priority = WorkPriority::p0; :>> owner = "claudeFable5"; :>> estimatedPoints = 3;
    }

    action def DeliveryRunS708 {
        action storyVerifyLadderStopsAtTheFirstRed;
        verification storyVerifyLadderStopsAtTheFirstRedDoD : Test { :>> id = "8bf81c85-c712-409a-b8df-624d52ecbd3c"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::test; :>> procedureText = "keel-cli/src/verify.rs orchestrates the five existing entry points as child processes of the running binary with inherited stdio, in the order validate, guard, clippy, probe, touched; a red rung stops the ladder and every later rung is recorded not-run; a probe rung with no --probe pair is recorded not-named and the ladder continues; --probe takes exactly two non-empty comma-separated shell-free command lines, both must exit 0, and the value is never mistaken for a root; --no-receipt forces the guard and touched rungs to run rather than answer from their receipts; the own-image refusal (issue150) is up front; every child has KEEL_PERF scrubbed. The receipt .keel/metrics/verify-receipt.toml carries head, at, seconds, outcome, stopped_at and one [[rung]] row each with name, verdict, exit, seconds, command, and round-trips through its parser. verify is a CliCommand in .engine/cli/commands.sysml, in CLI_FACTS and COMMAND_NAMES, dispatched in main.rs, so --help, dispatch and the facts agree (guard cli-surface-declared). The test-verify and delegated-ceremony skills and CLAUDE.md name the ladder instead of listing the rungs. Unit tests cover the stop, the green climb, the not-named pair, the pair's arity, the root resolution and the receipt round-trip. D0388 pair, run on the real tree from a copy of the binary: known-positive - with one clippy lint injected into keel-cli/src, `keel verify . --probe ...` stops at clippy within a minute of reaching that rung, the receipt says stopped_at = clippy with probe and touched not-run, and no test binary compiled; known-negative - with the lint removed, the same command climbs every rung green, writes verify-receipt.toml with stopped_at = none, and leaves touched-receipt.toml at the current code key so the next keel land skips what it observed."; }
    }

    verification verifyLadderStopsAtTheFirstRedRefineGate : Test { :>> id = "92dfd07a-a6a9-44b9-83b0-346431f187a5"; :>> title = "Sprint 708 refine gate (DoR)"; :>> createdAt = "2026-09-14"; :>> createdBy = "claudeFable5"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::inspect; :>> procedureText = "Chartered by D0476, accepted by the human 2026-09-14 with the process-change marker (a new command on the CLI surface; two skills and CLAUDE.md change meaning). Three points: one new module with its unit pair, the surface wiring in four homes, doc-sync, and two real-tree runs - the sprint-planning table puts a module with tests at 3. DoR: dcVerifyLadderStopsAtTheFirstRed ranks first on keel show whats-next after sprint707 closed at 1e2ed25 (declaration order is priority, D0052); the pair is the DoD's own; issue477 binds - no keel-cli/src or .engine edit while cargo or the ladder runs; the probe value is a command line and the root resolution must not consume it (repo_arg takes the first non-flag argument)."; }
