    part verifyLadderStopsAtTheFirstRedRefineGateR1 : TestResult { :>> id = "23ce1217-d230-46b2-85b1-3429a6936730"; :>> outcome = VerdictKind::proposed; :>> judgedAgainst = "1e2ed25"; :>> judgedAt = "2026-09-14"; :>> judgedBy = "claudeFable5"; }
    verification verifyLadderStopsAtTheFirstRedStandupGate : Test { :>> id = "8912ff9c-be81-45e3-b908-0ef9622d7a81"; :>> title = "Sprint 708 standup gate"; :>> createdAt = "2026-09-14"; :>> createdBy = "claudeFable5"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::inspect; :>> procedureText = "Order: verify.rs with its unit tests first (the climb is a pure function over a runner closure so the stop is tested without a child process); wire lib.rs, main.rs dispatch, COMMAND_NAMES, CLI_FACTS and commands.sysml together so cli-surface-declared judges all four at once; build, clippy -D warnings, keel sync-claude; --help and the --probe arity refusal from the copy; the capability_refusal_bites inventory test; doc-sync of test-verify (procedure and registry purpose), delegated-ceremony and CLAUDE.md sect.4/5; the sprint record before the real-tree runs because process-change is red until it exists (D0465) and the ladder will stop there; the known-positive with an injected lint, detached; remove the lint; the known-negative green ladder, detached; the gate results and the DoD result quoting both receipts; one CR: commit detached; keel-land; git status -sb and the CI conclusion read back."; }
    // RAN: Order followed as the standup names it with one correction recorded in the retro: verify.rs and its unit tests first; lib.rs, main.rs dispatch, COMMAND_NAMES 35, CLI_FACTS 86 and commands.sysml cliVerify wired together (scratch s708/wire.py); build, clippy, sync-claude; --help and the --probe arity refusal; capability_refusal_bites; doc-sync (test-verify SKILL.md 0.3.0 + registry purpose, delegated-ceremony, CLAUDE.md sect.4 and sect.5); the sprint record BEFORE the real-tree runs (the first known-positive launch stopped at guard: process-change red until the record existed, D0465); known-positive with the lint, lint removed, known-negative; issue477 held - no keel-cli/src or .engine edit while cargo or the ladder ran
    part verifyLadderStopsAtTheFirstRedStandupGateR1 : TestResult { :>> id = "8ed7d768-c0b0-4c95-ba0d-d19eee5244e6"; :>> outcome = VerdictKind::proposed; :>> judgedAgainst = "1e2ed25"; :>> judgedAt = "2026-09-14"; :>> judgedBy = "claudeFable5"; }
    verification verifyLadderStopsAtTheFirstRedImplementGate : Test { :>> id = "27322cc4-cc5e-4fc8-8492-a18e292b39dc"; :>> title = "Sprint 708 implement gate"; :>> createdAt = "2026-09-14"; :>> createdBy = "claudeFable5"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::test; :>> procedureText = "The implement gate holds when: cargo test --release --lib -- verify:: passes every unit test; cargo clippy --release --all-targets -- -D warnings exits 0; keel sync-claude --check reports the surface in step; keel verify --help renders from the fact and `keel verify . --probe onlyone` is refused with exit 2 naming the count; the capability_refusal_bites inventory test passes with verify in COMMAND_NAMES and the dispatch. Its evidence quotes those commands' own lines."; }
    // RAN: cargo test --release --lib -- verify:: -> 6 passed, 0 failed (a_red_rung_stops_the_ladder_before_the_test_binaries_compile, a_green_ladder_reaches_the_touched_run_last, an_unnamed_probe_pair_is_recorded_not_invented, probe_flag_takes_exactly_a_pair, the_probe_value_is_not_mistaken_for_a_root, receipt_round_trips); cargo clippy --release --all-targets -- -D warnings -> exit 0 after three fixes (missing_const_for_fn x2, unnecessary_debug_formatting); KEEL --help line 86 is verify [ROOT] [--probe POSITIVE,NEGATIVE] [--no-receipt]; KEEL verify . --probe onlyone -> --probe names 1 side(s); a D0388 pair is exactly two, exit=2; cargo test --release --test capability_refusal_bites -> 9 passed (the_command_inventory_matches_the_dispatch with verify); KEEL sync-claude --check . -> keel-owned subset matches this binary's generator (47 registry skill(s)); guard cli-surface-declared PASS 86 scanned
    part verifyLadderStopsAtTheFirstRedImplementGateR1 : TestResult { :>> id = "8ecddb11-de25-4149-94e8-a7bd18711110"; :>> outcome = VerdictKind::pass; :>> judgedAgainst = "1e2ed25"; :>> judgedAt = "2026-09-14"; :>> judgedBy = "claudeFable5"; }
    verification verifyLadderStopsAtTheFirstRedReviewGate : Test { :>> id = "e9ce247d-1d5d-4738-8181-ae5cecd6f5cc"; :>> title = "Sprint 708 review gate — three passes per D0172"; :>> createdAt = "2026-09-14"; :>> createdBy = "claudeFable5"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::inspect; :>> procedureText = "Three passes (D0172). Correctness: the ladder's order is a const array read by the climb, not five call sites; a red sets stopped_at and the loop records the rest not-run without asking them; the probe rung is not-named rather than pass when no pair is given, so a green receipt never claims a pair that was not run; both probe sides must exit 0. Honesty: the receipt names the command each rung ran, including the receipt-answering forms of guard and touched, so a reader can tell a receipt answer from a run; the exit code is the first red rung's own. Scope: the command adds no check (D0476 rationale) - gate check-engine and sync-claude --check stay outside the ladder and the test-verify skill says so; the full keel suite is untouched."; }
    // RAN: KEEL gate validate . -> 812 tracking file(s) validated clean.; KEEL gate check-engine . -> .engine instance files validated clean (kernel-free; D0112 phase 2).; KEEL gate guard --no-receipt . -> [guard] ALL PASS - 338 actionable warning(s) across 9 guard(s); exit=0 (process-change: locked edit authorised by d0476 cited as the charter of the co-committed sprint record, D0465; retro-backlog PASS after the retro named d0465 for its closed-in-sprint finding). Three passes per D0172 read against verify.rs: Rung::ORDER is the one order and climb() reads it; a red sets stopped_at and the loop records every later rung not-run without spawning it (unit a_red_rung_stops_the_ladder...); an absent pair is not-named, never pass; both probe sides must exit 0; every receipt row names the command it ran so a D0371 receipt answer is distinguishable from a run; exit code is the first red rung's own; check-engine and sync-claude --check stay outside the ladder and the test-verify skill says so
    part verifyLadderStopsAtTheFirstRedReviewGateR1 : TestResult { :>> id = "944b7f43-55f6-45c7-862d-4bb8bbf6fe38"; :>> outcome = VerdictKind::proposed; :>> judgedAgainst = "1e2ed25"; :>> judgedAt = "2026-09-14"; :>> judgedBy = "claudeFable5"; }
    verification verifyLadderStopsAtTheFirstRedCloseOutGate : Test { :>> id = "62565ec4-56cc-4570-89e2-465985880e83"; :>> title = "Sprint 708 closeOut gate (autonomous, D0049)"; :>> createdAt = "2026-09-14"; :>> createdBy = "claudeFable5"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::inspect; :>> procedureText = "Closes at the CR: commit that lands verify.rs, the four surface homes, the doc-sync, the regenerated .claude surface, the touched.rs land line naming nextest, and this record together: keel-land runs the touched set from that commit: a binary observed green at this content is skipped (D0474, code key 593ea821b10f6d8e from the green ladder), and one that reads this repo reruns because the tree key moved with the ceremony; gate validate / check-engine / guard --no-receipt green over that tree; dcVerifyLadderStopsAtTheFirstRedDoD carries a pass with both real-tree receipts quoted; the CI conclusion for the landing commit is read back as success; git status -sb shows main level with origin."; }
    verification verifyLadderStopsAtTheFirstRedRetroGate : Test { :>> id = "3a5039da-b641-4351-83b7-b6c7ab139c09"; :>> title = "Sprint 708 retro gate (autonomous, D0049)"; :>> createdAt = "2026-09-14"; :>> createdBy = "claudeFable5"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::analyze; :>> procedureText = "Avoidable issues scanned; findings are tracked items, not prose. The known-positive run before this record existed stopped at guard (process-change red, D0465) - the ladder did what it is for, and the order of the standup was corrected to record the sprint before the runs. Finding one, closed in-sprint: the known-positive run launched before this record existed stopped at guard (process-change red until the chartered sprint record is co-committed, D0465) - the ladder did what it is for; the standup's order was corrected to record the sprint before the runs. No new item - the control that caught it is d0465's process-change guard, already in force. Finding two, not reproduced: the validate rung took 34 s inside the first ladder against 0.4 s standalone; in the second known-positive and the known-negative ladders it took 0 s (verify-receipt rows), so no item - a single unrepeated reading is an observation, not a defect (D0151). Finding three, tracked: recording the implement gate result passed evidence with two backtick spans as a double-quoted shell argument and the shell emptied both (D0224, fifth occurrence) because record result and gate-result have no file form for --evidence - issue543, resolver dcEvidenceGoesThroughAFile, ranked third. Finding four, tracked: while this sprint ran, the CI conclusion for 1e2ed25 (sprint707) was read back as failure - nextest --workspace lists keel-parser four harness = false binaries the keel-cli-only exclusion missed; sprint707 retro had dismissed that drift and its closeOut clause naming CI success is false - issue542, resolver dcCiNextestExcludesEveryCustomHarness, ranked second."; }
